{"tag":"9IUL","kind":"statement","subkind":"theorem","paper":"math/9801068","version":"3","local":"theorem-1","file":"","number":"1","section":"sec-1","order":1,"title":"Theorem","body_md":"Fix $\\epsilon \u003e 0$.  Then for all sufficiently large $n$,\nall but an $\\epsilon$ fraction of the domino tilings\nof the Aztec diamond of order $n$\nwill have a temperate zone whose boundary \nstays uniformly within distance $\\epsilon n$\nof the inscribed circle.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"theorem","item":"statement/theorem","head":"environment","counter":"theorem","number_from":"render","scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Jockusch-Propp-Shor.tex","from":320,"to":327},"hash":"sha256:7e7260d620e6d54ed4a99b647054ffff2460bbdd884b00b3d5be270c7c741585","minhash":"","census":"math/9801068v3#env-1","extractor":"ax/v0.5.2"}
{"tag":"5PA3","kind":"statement","subkind":"theorem","paper":"math/9801068","version":"3","local":"theorem-2","file":"","number":"2","section":"sec-1","order":2,"title":"Theorem","body_md":"Fix $\\alpha \\leq \\beta$.\nIf one runs the exclusion process\nstarting from the state $x^*$,\nthen the number of particles in the interval $[\\alpha n, \\beta n]$\nat time $n$, normalized by dividing by $n$,\nconverges in probability to $h(\\alpha)-h(\\beta)$, where\n\\[\nh(u) = \\left\\{ \\begin{array}{ll}\n\t-u \u0026 \n\t\t\\text{for $u\u003c-\\frac12$,} \\\\\n\t{\\scriptstyle \\frac{1-u}{2} - \\frac12 \\sqrt{\\frac12-u^2}} \u0026 \n\t\t\\text{for $-\\frac12 \\leq u \\leq \\frac12$, and} \\\\\n\t0 \u0026 \\text{for $u\u003e\\frac12$}. \\end{array} \\right.\n\\]","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"theorem","item":"statement/theorem","head":"environment","counter":"theorem","number_from":"render","scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Jockusch-Propp-Shor.tex","from":378,"to":393},"hash":"sha256:778daa0e0bb8e5f3286d09039b12d6f5e19762d11ca2e386abcfe9c11273e4af","minhash":"","census":"math/9801068v3#env-2","extractor":"ax/v0.5.2"}
{"tag":"S0OW","kind":"statement","subkind":"theorem","paper":"math/9801068","version":"3","local":"theorem-3","file":"","number":"3","section":"sec-1","order":3,"title":"Theorem","body_md":"The translation-invariant, stationary probability measures on ${\\cal X}$\nare precisely those that can be expressed as\nconvex combinations of the measures $\\mu_d$,\n$0 \\leq d \\leq 1$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"theorem","item":"statement/theorem","head":"environment","counter":"theorem","number_from":"render","scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Jockusch-Propp-Shor.tex","from":491,"to":496},"hash":"sha256:c3778cfae4f7e2f1c4a9328b5a1c97b8c2b3e76e814f756a1aa76cac11ab152b","minhash":"","census":"math/9801068v3#env-3","extractor":"ax/v0.5.2"}
{"tag":"LE2E","kind":"statement","subkind":"proposition","paper":"math/9801068","version":"3","local":"proposition-1","file":"","label":"prop1","number":"5.1","section":"sec-7","order":4,"title":"Proposition","body_md":"\\label{prop1}\nFor all non-negative integers $m,n$ and integers $k,l$, \none has \n\\begin{equation*}\n{\\cal L}(S(k,m)) * {\\cal L}(S(l,n)) \\geq {\\cal L}(S(k+l,m+n)).\n\\end{equation*}","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"proposition","item":"statement/proposition","head":"environment","counter":"proposition","number_from":"render","labels":["prop1"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Jockusch-Propp-Shor.tex","from":1827,"to":1834},"hash":"sha256:846e48004e68a87bee5539315f95a048ccbb856d56d2dafe03f91c3f3e94c612","minhash":"","census":"math/9801068v3#env-4","extractor":"ax/v0.5.2"}
{"tag":"WLUF","kind":"statement","subkind":"proposition","paper":"math/9801068","version":"3","local":"proposition-2","file":"","label":"prop2","number":"5.2","section":"sec-7","order":5,"title":"Proposition","body_md":"\\label{prop2}\nFor all $u \\in {\\mathds R}$,\nthe random variables $\\frac1n S(\\lfloor un \\rfloor,n)$\nconverge almost surely and in $L^1$ to\na constant $h(u)$ as $n \\rightarrow \\infty$.\nThe function $h$ is decreasing and convex;\n$h(u)=0$ for $u \u003e \\frac12$ and\n$h(u)=-u$ for $u \u003c -\\frac12$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"proposition","item":"statement/proposition","head":"environment","counter":"proposition","number_from":"render","labels":["prop2"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Jockusch-Propp-Shor.tex","from":1869,"to":1878},"hash":"sha256:3ae04cbae56338678ab2c4ea22b2d4bdaed7cb7275f24cbe5b3070b491106d5a","minhash":"","census":"math/9801068v3#env-5","extractor":"ax/v0.5.2"}
{"tag":"GOR5","kind":"statement","subkind":"proposition","paper":"math/9801068","version":"3","local":"proposition-3","file":"","label":"prop3","number":"5.3","section":"sec-7","order":6,"title":"Proposition","body_md":"\\label{prop3}\nIf $h$ is differentiable at $u$, then\n${\\cal E} X(k,n) \\rightarrow -h'(u)$\nwhenever $n \\rightarrow \\infty$ with $k/n \\rightarrow u$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"proposition","item":"statement/proposition","head":"environment","counter":"proposition","number_from":"render","labels":["prop3"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Jockusch-Propp-Shor.tex","from":1905,"to":1910},"hash":"sha256:c11111ad8208a92d79f5b35e074f215b78b6d89aa5d2567b8af79745bf1b1d59","minhash":"","census":"math/9801068v3#env-6","extractor":"ax/v0.5.2"}
{"tag":"J4B4","kind":"statement","subkind":"proposition","paper":"math/9801068","version":"3","local":"proposition-4","file":"","label":"prop4","number":"5.4","section":"sec-7","order":7,"title":"Proposition","body_md":"\\label{prop4}\nFor all $k \\in {\\mathds Z}$ and $m,n \\in {\\mathds N}$\nwe have\n\\begin{align}\n\\mu(k,n) \u0026\\geq \\mu(k+1,n), \n\t\\label{twelve} \\\\\n\\mu(k,n+m) \u0026\\leq \\sum_l \\beta(m,l) \\mu(k-l,n), \\ \\text{and} \n\t\\label{thirteena} \\\\\n\\mu(k,n+m) \u0026\\geq \\sum_l \\beta(m,l) \\mu(k+l,n), \n\t\\label{thirteenb}\n\\end{align}\nwhere $\\beta(m,\\cdot)$ is the binomial distribution\nwith mean $\\frac m 2$ and variance $\\frac m 4$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"proposition","item":"statement/proposition","head":"environment","counter":"proposition","number_from":"render","labels":["prop4","twelve","thirteena","thirteenb"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Jockusch-Propp-Shor.tex","from":1945,"to":1959},"hash":"sha256:61c9ebf9c1ae8d652d5d3e70681d97930beced69dcbe59cff34544d8b3fdaa63","minhash":"","census":"math/9801068v3#env-7","extractor":"ax/v0.5.2"}
{"tag":"HQU7","kind":"statement","subkind":"proposition","paper":"math/9801068","version":"3","local":"proposition-5","file":"","label":"prop5","number":"5.5","section":"sec-7","order":8,"title":"Proposition","body_md":"\\label{prop5}\nIf $h$ is differentiable at $v$,\nany weak limit $\\mu^*$ of the measures $\\mu(\\lfloor un \\rfloor , n)$, \n$n \\rightarrow \\infty$, is of the form\n\\begin{equation*}\n\\mu^* = \\int_0^1 \\mu_t \\, \\rho(dt)\n\\end{equation*}\nwith $\\rho$ some probability distribution on $[0,1]$,\nand with $\\mu_t$ defined as in section~\\ref{sec:reduction}~(there we called it $\\mu_d$).","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"proposition","item":"statement/proposition","head":"environment","counter":"proposition","number_from":"render","labels":["prop5"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Jockusch-Propp-Shor.tex","from":1980,"to":1990},"hash":"sha256:26a31d13e8f132c2f5e88fe8d41254466cc32b2f4f301d04e8cc78204ef29fe2","minhash":"","census":"math/9801068v3#env-8","extractor":"ax/v0.5.2"}
{"tag":"LG4G","kind":"statement","subkind":"proposition","paper":"math/9801068","version":"3","local":"proposition-6","file":"","label":"prop6","number":"5.6","section":"sec-7","order":9,"title":"Proposition","body_md":"\\label{prop6}\nAssume $h$ is differentiable at ${\\overline{u}}$.\nFor any finite set $F$ of cardinality $n$ and any $\\epsilon \u003e 0$\nthere exists a $\\delta \u003e 0$ and $n_0 \\in {\\mathds N}$ such that\n\\begin{equation}\n\\label{sixteen}\n|\\rho(\\lfloor un \\rfloor,F;n)-\\rho(\\lfloor {\\overline{u}} n \\rfloor,F;n)| \n\\leq \\epsilon\n\\end{equation}\nfor $|u - {\\overline{u}} | \\leq \\delta$ and $n \\geq n_0$, and\n\\begin{equation}\n\\label{seventeen}\n|\\rho(\\lfloor {\\overline{u}} n \\rfloor,F;n+m)-\n\\rho(\\lfloor {\\overline{u}} n \\rfloor,F;n)| \n\\leq \\epsilon\n\\end{equation}\nfor $0 \\leq m \\leq \\delta n$ and $n \\geq n_0$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"proposition","item":"statement/proposition","head":"environment","counter":"proposition","number_from":"render","labels":["prop6","sixteen","seventeen"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Jockusch-Propp-Shor.tex","from":2014,"to":2032},"hash":"sha256:d6e8412ac4aa3cad7a69799540ec5f03802da64da7770ef55115921a59e9caab","minhash":"","census":"math/9801068v3#env-9","extractor":"ax/v0.5.2"}
{"tag":"1BRG","kind":"statement","subkind":"proposition","paper":"math/9801068","version":"3","local":"proposition-7","file":"","label":"prop7","number":"6.1","section":"sec-9","order":10,"title":"Proposition","body_md":"\\label{prop7}\n$h(u) \\geq \\frac{1-u}{2} - \\frac12 \\sqrt{\\frac12 - u^2}$\nfor $|u| \\leq \\frac12$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"proposition","item":"statement/proposition","head":"environment","counter":"proposition","number_from":"render","labels":["prop7"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Jockusch-Propp-Shor.tex","from":2106,"to":2110},"hash":"sha256:9fe02ab83516d70b5ea92fbc5506c915da1aa9a6f5c27553ca2b659fd201ba16","minhash":"","census":"math/9801068v3#env-10","extractor":"ax/v0.5.2"}
{"tag":"P77A","kind":"statement","subkind":"proposition","paper":"math/9801068","version":"3","local":"proposition-8","file":"","label":"prop8","number":"6.2","section":"sec-10","order":11,"title":"Proposition","body_md":"\\label{prop8}\n$h(u) \\leq \\frac{1-u}{2} - \\frac12 \\sqrt{\\frac12 - u^2}$\nfor $|u| \\leq \\frac12$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"proposition","item":"statement/proposition","head":"environment","counter":"proposition","number_from":"render","labels":["prop8"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Jockusch-Propp-Shor.tex","from":2225,"to":2229},"hash":"sha256:9c1726ed31fcae4296e5fdc1c9d120c660be71adf5ad01e327d4100f8689f41e","minhash":"","census":"math/9801068v3#env-11","extractor":"ax/v0.5.2"}
{"tag":"J3IA","kind":"remark","subkind":"unknown","paper":"math/9801068","version":"3","local":"ack-1","file":"","section":"sec-13","order":12,"title":"W","body_md":"e thank David Aldous and Persi Diaconis for helpful conversations.\nThanks also to Sameera Iyengar, who wrote the first program\nfor generating random domino tilings by the shuffling algorithm.\nWe are also grateful to the anonymous referee who made many helpful suggestions.\n\n\\","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"ack","item":"unknown","head":"environment","scope":"paper","origin":"own","span":{"file":"Jockusch-Propp-Shor.tex","from":2599,"to":2606},"hash":"sha256:0245cc9254e9a87de35e78bc887849f2b8aada4403225989e09b6ad135b2d1a3","minhash":"","census":"math/9801068v3#env-12","extractor":"ax/v0.5.2"}
